Hi,

I am trying to model a data set consisting of ARUs that were deployed and retrieved between June 26th-October 5th. Observation data consists of 0, 1, and NAs. Some sites were deployed and retrieved at different times which makes the observation data full of NAs. Can unmarked handle only  a certain amount of NAs? When I run a null model from a umf data frame:
Data1<- unmarkedMultFrame(y=y, siteCovs=site.cov, numPrimary=104,
                                       yearlySiteCovs = list(Julian_Day= Julian_Day))

p.m0.subset1<-colext(psiformula = ~1, gammaformula = ~1, epsilonformula = ~1, pformula = ~1, data=Data1)

I get an error:

Error in optim(starts, nll, method = method, hessian = getHessian, ...) :
  initial value in 'vmmin' is not finite

y <- 1872 (104 days x 18 hours) (note first few hours on day one are all NAs but I need the NA hours due to dimension requirements)
S<- nrow(y) #29 sites
J <- 18 #secondary periods in hours
T <- 104 primary periods in days or seasons

Yearly site covs= Julian date 176-279 (104 repeated columns with 29 rows)

However, when I run subsets of data: the first 31 days, then the next 31 days, and the following 42 days they work while dropping sites that have too many NAs ( I am assuming)....

Why can't unmarked handle my full data set?

Thank you!

Ashley

